n\n## What I measured\n\n262 narrowing mutants of my own, each a byte-offset edit into production, PRESENT-asserted, driven through the whole package suite, restored with a sha256 check. Kills whose only failing tests were the source-text censuses are scored `census-only`, never as behavioural kills — every identity mutant reddens `TestIdentityGatesAreCensused` by construction, and that would have inflated the score by 39.\n\n| Battery | applied | behavioural kills | survived |\n| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n| `require*`, both edges, all 19 call sites | 35 | 33 | 2 |\n| `check*`, every literal edge | 68 | 60 | 8 |\n| `len` guards + environment rows | 22 | 19 | 1 |\n| identity NEQ, both sides, all 62 rows | 119 | 73 | 0 |\n| `==`-spelled gates + typed re-runs | 18 | 13 | 2 |\n\n**G-A passes, both classes.** All 19 `require*` sites die at both edges — the wrapper is measured everywhere it is called, not pinned per-caller-and-hoped. 54 of 54 driven identity rows behaviourally killed, zero survivors, and none of the 8 exemptions is one a test would have caught. Of 13 survivors, 11 trace to a committed registry row whose rationale I checked against the code rather than took on faith (`parseUint53Literal` really does refuse past 2⁵³−1; `scalar.ParsePlatform` really does make the platform edges unreachable).\n\n**G-B passes.** Zero production bytes changed between rev4 and rev5 — `git diff 1469c634 c0174e87 -- '*.go' ':(exclude)*_test.go'` is empty. Resurrection is impossible by construction. N8 is genuinely fixed.\n\n## Why it's not accepted\n\nThree findings, all in the new instruments rather than in shipped behaviour:\n\n- **F2** (`repeat-of: rev4/N8`) — `scanBoundSiteIDs` matches `call.Fun.(*ast.Ident)` only and scans `len` guards only inside `if` conditions, under the flat sentence \"a new bound with no row fails the census\". Three token-preserving plants pass the whole suite, and the first is `var zzprobeIndirect = requireStringBounds` — literally the shape they fixed for the constructor census *in this same commit*.\n- **F1** — the identity census is `token.NEQ`-only under the same unqualified sentence, while `discovery.go:105` and `:112` are live zero-fact refusals spelled `== \"\"`. Both are behaviourally covered today; the gate isn't.\n- **F3** — widening `CapabilityUsable`/`capabilityMapUsable`'s status clause to admit `conditional` leaves the full suite green at both sites. These gate `CheckTargetWriteGates`. I think it's equivalent via the decode-side coherence gate, but nothing says so anywhere.\n\nThe current denominators are complete — an independent any-shape scan finds 58 helper calls and the census derives 58 — so nothing ships unmeasured. What fails open is the instrument the next two leaves inherit, which is exactly what the brief said this leaf is establishing.\n\nOne thing I deliberately didn't do: `LOGBOOK.md` is inside the candidate tree, so the logbook entry belongs to the producer's rework, not to me. Findings are on the board in `TASK-260830-2z3se0_review-verdict-rev5.md` and `_review-mutation-log-rev5.md` (per-mutant, with named killers).","ttft_ms":2052,"type":"result","duration_ms":1763222,"uuid":"fe1e1b09-761f-451a-b1c3-7520996d72c2","ttft_stream_ms":1224,"time_to_request_ms":27,"first_content_frame_ms":1224,"queued_turn_count":0}
